  <reporting-org ref="US-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Agency for International Development</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Small Town WASH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  ...With FY 2022 funds this activity will: .Expand access to water and sanitation facilities and improve the governance of water resources in small communities in Borno, Adamawa, and Yobe (BAY) in Northeast Nigeria and Abia, Delta, and Imo State in the southern part of the country; and. Funds will be utilized for on-going construction in the Northeast, and will mobilize resources to the south of Nigeria to improve the water treatment plants in Abia, Delta and Imo states. .This activity will provide technical assistance, address immediate sanitation needs and challenges related to Fecal Sludge Management (FSM) by supporting the construction of a Fecal Sludge Treatment Facility and strengthening Emergency FSM models and rehabilitate three water supply systems to supply water to approximately 60,000 households in Abia, Imo, and Delta states. This activity will facilitate the economic recovery of some crisis-affected communities and bolster the capacity of the state governments in providing essential WASH services by creating and sustaining enabling environments for Small Towns Water Supply and Sanitation Agencies and Water Consumers Associations to operate effectively. The activity will support climate change adaptation or mitigation objectives in its water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) programming..This activity contributes to the CDCS Development Objective 1: Broadened and Inclusive Economic Growth and Intermediate Result (IR) 1.4: Water resource management and services improved. This activity links directly to JSP Goals 1 and 2 and water strategies... .</narrative>
  </description>
